# RBAC and Data Integrity

Only these roles exist. Do not add extra roles unless the product owner expands the matrix.

| Role | Actor | Scope |
| SUPER_ADMIN | UNICEF Country Office / senior programme managers | All 20 kindergartens: users, frameworks, aggregates, configuration |
| KINDERGARTEN_MANAGER | Local director | One assigned facility: site data, staff, inventory |
| FIELD_MONITOR | Field officer | Assigned sites: submit official evaluation forms and facility audits |
| COUNCIL_MEMBER | Parents and Teachers Council | Own kindergarten: periodic council evaluation forms only |
| DISTRICT_EDUCATION | District education plan (پلانی پەروەردەی قەزا) | Kindergartens whose `education_directorate_id` matches the user’s district: **read-only** (no writes, no form submit) |

## Enforcement

- Server-side on every query/mutation. Hidden UI is not authorization.
- `SUPER_ADMIN` may omit `kindergartenId`. Every other role **must** be scoped to assigned site(s); missing scope → 403.
- `KINDERGARTEN_MANAGER` and `COUNCIL_MEMBER` bind to one `users.kindergarten_id`.
- `FIELD_MONITOR` binds via `user_site_assignments` (one or many sites).
- `DISTRICT_EDUCATION` binds to `users.education_directorate_id` and sees every kindergarten in that district; mutations fail closed.
- Soft-delete child records. Immutable `audit_logs` on all writes.
- Fail closed: never return an unscoped list when the actor is site-bound.
